{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00134",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.0,
      "end_seconds": 6.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Afternoon, doctor. They're in and comfortable, and I have the measurements ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.26,
      "end_seconds": 11.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Thanks, that's helpful. Hello, please sit. What's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.95,
      "end_seconds": 17.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "Doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.54,
      "end_seconds": 23.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.32,
      "end_seconds": 33.12,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Honestly, it's sharp pain in the left chest when I breathe in, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.05,
      "end_seconds": 35.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "When did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.53,
      "end_seconds": 39.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Since last weekend, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.19,
      "end_seconds": 43.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.98,
      "end_seconds": 44.94,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.77,
      "end_seconds": 49.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.2,
      "end_seconds": 62.71,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a low fever a few days ago as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.43,
      "end_seconds": 69.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 69.69,
      "end_seconds": 75.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.59,
      "end_seconds": 84.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on. Is it constant, or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.11,
      "end_seconds": 92.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "It's every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.73,
      "end_seconds": 97.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.72,
      "end_seconds": 111.13,
      "duration_seconds": 12.41,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.54,
      "end_seconds": 120.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 120.73,
      "end_seconds": 123.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "She takes apixaban, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.3,
      "end_seconds": 127.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 128.19,
      "end_seconds": 137.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.98,
      "text": "5 milligrams. She is on ibuprofen, 400 milligrams, when it hurts, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.34,
      "end_seconds": 142.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "I was on diclofenac before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.52,
      "end_seconds": 164.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Tell me about your health in general, any ongoing conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.6,
      "end_seconds": 183.3,
      "duration_seconds": 16.7,
      "text": "Yes, arthritis in my knees. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. I've had an irregular heartbeat, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.86,
      "end_seconds": 193.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.52,
      "text": "Okay, I can see arthritis in your knees in your file as well. Anything special about your diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.23,
      "end_seconds": 197.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "I try to avoid too much sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.49,
      "end_seconds": 202.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Alright, are you active at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.16,
      "end_seconds": 207.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Barely, I'm mostly sedentary these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.99,
      "end_seconds": 212.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Okay, have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.96,
      "end_seconds": 218.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Oh, I had a hernia repair about five years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.69,
      "end_seconds": 222.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "So, how about leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.48,
      "end_seconds": 226.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Not at all, no leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.41,
      "end_seconds": 232.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Did you get palpitations or injury to the chest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.46,
      "end_seconds": 247.68,
      "duration_seconds": 14.22,
      "text": "So, no, no palpitations, no injury to the chest. I did have aching all over at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.1,
      "end_seconds": 256.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Have you noticed recent long travel, breathlessness at rest or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.27,
      "end_seconds": 263.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "No, no recent long travel, breathlessness at rest or coughing up blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.88,
      "end_seconds": 267.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.28,
      "end_seconds": 270.25,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.04,
      "end_seconds": 272.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.93,
      "end_seconds": 275.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 277.26,
      "end_seconds": 289.26,
      "duration_seconds": 12.0,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Oxygen saturation is 98 percent, BP is 108 over 77, temperature is 36.7 degrees, pulse 65, respiratory rate 17."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.3,
      "end_seconds": 292.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.25,
      "end_seconds": 296.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "If you're comfortable, I'll examine you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.08,
      "end_seconds": 300.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Almost done with this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.53,
      "end_seconds": 310.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Air entry is equal on both sides."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.17,
      "end_seconds": 314.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Almost done with this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.34,
      "end_seconds": 328.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "I can hear a faint rub on the left side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.53,
      "end_seconds": 334.43,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Okay, finished."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.49,
      "end_seconds": 373.04,
      "duration_seconds": 28.55,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, it fits best with viral pleurisy. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. It could also be a chest infection, so we'll keep that open. We shouldn't forget a clot in the lung that we should rule out. Regular pain relief makes it easier to take deep breaths, which protects the lung. Right, look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.88,
      "end_seconds": 379.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "No questions. Thank you."
    }
  ]
}